  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since&nbsp;the intensity at the central maxima remains unchanged, the change in the path difference&nbsp;should be an integral multiple of the wavelength. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
